Z||000000||Philphine||09-18-2000||01:33 AM||||<BR>not sure if i should switch this to the tech section.<P>got some time to play with my "cheap thrill" (i've decided to name it) fiero. the battery was dead again. since it and the alternator are new something i'm sure is draining it. since i'm guessing the assesories that work aren't shorted i started with disconnecting the non working headlight motor on the drivers side. my thinking is that even though it's not working it may still be drawing voltage. i put the passenger side in the up position and disconnected it too so they match. i'll live with the "bug eye" look for a while. the other non working item was the radio. no diplay or sound but a thump when you push the power button. i stuck the radio out of my '87 in for now, so i have sound and could try the speakers, they all work.<P>had a brake problem the first time i drove last week. one caliper started to lock up then i lost the brakes, pedal sank to the floor. today the brakes were back so i threw caution to the wind and drove it again but stayed closer to home (i couldn't help myself. i drove it to circuit city to work up a stereo idea). brakes stayed but i'm expecting about another $100 on brake work (flex lines, pads etc.) engine ran fine.<P>stopped to put air in tires and noticed they look like they won't last long plenty of thread but kind of rotted.  i'm hoping to find a cavalier z24 rim to round out a set i have plus a couple of tires so i can switch to 16's cheap for now. if i can get the tire size i want for now i can put them on the style wheel i like later instead of getting 14's now that i wouldn't want to keep.<P>took the luggage rack off. i guess it's better to find another trunk without it but since it needs a paint job any way it's cheaper to just flll in the holes. hopefully a mustang f40 wing will take it's place.<P>drivers side rear view mirror glass was out and in car so i epoxied it back. couple of bucks for epoxy is my only cost this go round.<P><BR>i notice each time i work on it that it seems to be in pretty good shape. it must have been well cared for up to the time it broke down, then was neglected.<P> <BR>it's a 3 stage project now. first get it running and driving reliably and see how little i can spend doing it. then some fixing up, which will blow that buget (stereo, wing, wheels {which will kind of cross the line bettween making it driveable and personalizing it} etc.). last, i'm hoping i can make it a convertible.<P>long post i know but i thought i'd try mapping out my progress. <BR>  <P>------------------<BR>Phil T<P>'87 coupe (feral)<BR>'84 indy<BR>'84 coupe (cheap thrill)<P>[This message has been edited by Philphine (edited 09-18-2000).]<p>[This message has been edited by Philphine (edited 09-18-2000).]||||reg||1
